WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.350
Speaker 1: Mitt Romney was asked the other
day, will you vote for Trump if he's the 2024

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:07.350
Republican nominee?

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:09.660
This is an interesting question because there
are many Republicans who are starting to say

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.179
things like, I would rather a different nominee.

00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:16.119
I would prefer that we just nominate someone
different and that it not be up to me to decide

00:00:16.119 --> 00:00:17.119
on Election Day.

00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:18.270
Do I vote for Trump or not?

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:19.960
Let's just pick a different nominee.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:24.849
Mitt Romney is speaking with a clarity that
many Republicans are not speaking with.

00:00:24.849 --> 00:00:29.179
Now, this is not a look at how great Mitt
Romney is story.

00:00:29.179 --> 00:00:32.150
This is a look at how low the bar is story.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:36.320
Mitt Romney is clearly saying I would not
support Trump even if he were the nominee

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.320
in 2024.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.160
Speaker 3: It's going to be hard to knock
him off as our nominee.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.350
If he became a nominee, I think he loses again.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.620
Speaker 4: And would you support him if he's
the nominee?

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.850
Speaker 3: Absolutely not.

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:48.410
And I mean, I get asked that.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:49.550
I mean.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.410
Speaker 2: Look.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:54.610
Speaker 3: I voted to remove him from office
twice, so.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:58.160
Speaker 4: I knew what your answer is going
to be had I had.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.680
Speaker 3: But the answer is and it's not
just because he he loses.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:07.860
I mean, that's that's my reason that I offer
to other people who are big fans of his.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:13.070
But but it's also he's he's simply not a person
who ought to have the reigns of the government,

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:14.070
the United States.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:15.070
Speaker 1: Okay.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:16.070
Very, very clear.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:18.410
Romney says it's not just about I'd rather
a different nominee.

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.110
If he's the nominee, I'm not voting for him.

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:24.430
Compare and contrast this with some of the
more spineless people in the Republican Party.

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:25.500
William Barr.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:30.890
William Barr, one of Trump's former attorney
generals attorneys general, said this guy

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:34.470
was a threat to democracy, all these horrible,
horrible things.

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:35.470
But I don't know.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.120
I mean, if he's a Democrat, I might still
have to vote for him.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.120
Listen to this.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:42.430
Speaker 5: Well, I certainly have made it
clear I don't think he should be our nominee.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:45.869
And I'm going to, you know, support somebody
else for the nominee.

00:01:45.869 --> 00:01:50.760
Speaker 4: But if he is the nominee and you
have your choices, Donald Trump or whoever

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.350
is running on the Democratic side, would you
vote for him?

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:58.350
Speaker 5: Because I believe that the greatest
threat to the country is the progressive agenda

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.570
being pushed by the Democratic Party.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:03.960
It's inconceivable to me that I wouldn't vote
for the Republican nominee.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:04.970
Speaker 2: Wow.

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:05.979
Speaker 1: Wow.

00:02:05.979 --> 00:02:07.450
Threat to democracy.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.729
Dangerous.

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:11.620
No business has no clue what's going on.

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:13.520
But I mean a savannah, please.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:14.520
A Democrat.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:15.990
I'm not going to vote for a Democrat.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:17.630
That would be even worse.

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:23.590
And then Mitch McConnell, even who Trump has
called his wife, I don't remember if Trump

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:27.190
called his wife ugly, but he certainly called
her different names, has attacked him as a

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:30.920
rhino just up and down, slamming McConnell.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:34.640
Even McConnell, what was it, ten days ago
when he was asked?

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:36.450
He played coy with it and didn't rule it out.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:41.450
Speaker 2: In light of what you said, that
there's no room in your party for anyone who

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:43.750
covers these, I submit to you, if Donald Trump
wins the Republican nomination, would you

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:44.750
support him?

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:52.480
Speaker 6: Look, let me just say again, there
is simply no room in the Republican Party

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:57.519
